  provenance: "AUTHORED looks (slice 6, G30). Code-built particle systems on DeepWater/General
    Quarters/Particle (HDRP). HD_Naval_Explosion and the VFX Arsenal flames were
    tried first and did not fit: the built-in particle shader draws untextured quads
    under HDRP, and the flames are about a metre across and too dim under daylight
    exposure.\nPublic: Phalanx 4,500 rounds/min in 100-round bursts (1.33 s), 115\xB0/s
    train and 86\xB0/s elevation; Mk 38 180 rounds/min. Measured on the Blender model:
    Mk 45 barrel 7.1 m, CIWS 2.4 m, Mk 38 3.6 m; waterline 141 m.\nSounds: VLS launch
    and detonation are the repo's FDS recordings; the rest are synthesised stand-ins
    (G32) until recordings are dropped in."
